  "facts": [
    "The Newburgh–Beacon Bridge opened its original northern span on November 2, 1963, as a two‑lane continuous truss, later expanded to three lanes per direction after a 1980 parallel span was added.",
    "In 1981, the eastbound span became the United States' second interstate‑funded bike path, featuring a dedicated bicycle lane that opened just a year after the new span's inauguration.",
    "The bridge’s 2,204‑foot cantilever main span, with a 1,000‑foot center, was engineered by Modjeski & Masters and constructed by Bethlehem Steel, making it a landmark of mid‑century American bridge design."
